  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Added pure-Rust machine tool-table codecs in `crates/tools/src/` (`tool_table.rs`, `tool_table_xml.rs`, `tool_table_pathpilot.rs`, `tool_table_pathpilot_desc.rs`, `tool_table_hurco.rs`) with no new crate dependencies.\n- Added `crates/app/src/tool_table.rs` to detect formats (`auto`, `camtools`, `pathpilot`, `hurco`) and convert lengths with document or explicit units.\n- Extended `LibraryTool` with `number: Option<u32>` and split `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs` into `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import/{mod.rs,report.rs}` to preserve controller `T<n>` numbers, refuse number clashes, allow swaps within Update/Replace imports, and keep one undo step.\n- Updated `import_tool_library` and `export_tool_library` in `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `cam.importTools` and `cam.exportTools` in `crates/app/src/script/{api,mod}.rs`, `assets/scripts/cam.d.ts`, and `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`.\n- Updated `crates/ui/src/state_tool_library.rs` and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_library.rs` file filters and actions for `.camtools`, `.csv`, and `.TCM` in the active document units.\n- Documented PathPilot and Hurco workflows and refusals in `site/content/guide/` (`set-up/tools.md`, `check-and-post/machines.md`, `automate/mcp.md`, `automate/cli.md`) and added `docs/decisions/2566-machine-tool-tables.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nCamCraft only supported its native `.camtools` JSON format. Users could not exchange Tormach PathPilot `.csv` tool tables or Hurco WinMax `.TCM` XML libraries, and imports always ignored controller `T<n>` numbers.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pinning suites:\n  - `crates/tools/tests/tool_table.rs` (5 tests: `detects_formats_by_extension_and_content`, `pathpilot_parses_sample_and_ignores_placeholder_z_offset_and_negative_probe_marker`, `pathpilot_refuses_bad_headers_bad_rows_and_non_mill_export`, `hurco_maps_supported_types_and_refuses_unsupported_by_name`, `hurco_export_roundtrips_and_escapes_xml_without_control_state`)\n  - `crates/app/tests/tool_table.rs` (failed 3/3 before the fix; passed 5/5 after: `pathpilot_csv_imports_with_numbers_diameters_undo_and_roundtrips`, `hurco_tcm_imports_with_numbers_kinds_diameters_gauge_lengths_and_exports_without_control_state`, `unsupported_hurco_tool_type_and_bad_pathpilot_rows_are_refused_by_name`, `controller_number_conflicts_refuse_in_add_mode_and_swap_in_replace_or_update`, `script_verbs_roundtrip_pathpilot_csv_and_hurco_tcm`)\n  - `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_import.rs` (`state_imports_and_exports_pathpilot_csv_and_hurco_tcm_in_document_units`)\n  - `site/tests/test_guide_after_1995.py` (6/6 passed, including `test_tools_page_covers_pathpilot_and_hurco_tool_tables`)\n- Mutation checks:\n  - Reverted `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` and `crates/app/src/script/api.rs` to `upstream/main`: `pathpilot_csv_imports_with_numbers_diameters_undo_and_roundtrips` failed (`unknown argument \"units\"`), passed after restore.\n  - Changed the `map_hurco_type` catch-all in `crates/tools/src/tool_table_hurco.rs` to return `EndMill`: `hurco_maps_supported_types_and_refuses_unsupported_by_name` failed, passed after restore.\n  - Changed `claim_number` in `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import/mod.rs` to skip clash checks: `controller_number_conflicts_refuse_in_add_mode_and_swap_in_replace_or_update` failed, passed after restore.\n  - Changed `is_mill_table_kind` in `crates/tools/src/tool_table_pathpilot.rs` to return `true`: `pathpilot_refuses_bad_headers_bad_rows_and_non_mill_export` failed, passed after restore.\n- Gate and clippy:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 61 steps passed, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: 0 warnings, 0 errors.\n\n## UI screenshots\n\nThese images show the import and export help in the shipping Tool library.\nThey use the real egui layout, fonts, icons, textures, and paint output, rendered in software.\nBefore uses `upstream/main` at `3a240b7fb2a784037ec951e0b2f2d72ae57acbc6`.\nAfter uses this PR's Tool library code.\nThe images are on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\nNo image or capture code is in the PR branch.\nNative OS dialog capture was unavailable on this host. The GPU had no adapter, and display capture failed.\n\n| Control | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Import library help | ![Import library before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2641/import-before.png) | ![Import library after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2641/import-after.png) |\n| Export library help | ![Export library before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2641/export-before.png) | ![Export library after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2641/export-after.png) |\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nnone\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Live tool table import on a Tormach PathPilot controller or PathPilot Hub UI.\n- Live import of CamCraft partial `.TCM` exports on a Hurco WinMax 9.01 control.\n- `zola build` site checks (`test_guide_icons.py`, `test_guide_images.py`, `test_guide_navigation.py`, `test_operation_reference.py`, `test_windows_troubleshooting.py`) because `zola` is not installed in this environment (all 35 non-zola site tests passed).\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch other functions or lines in shared files; whichever merges second refreshes:\n- `#2618` (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`)\n- `#2563` (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, `crates/app/src/lib.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `crates/app/src/script/api.rs`)\n- `#2554` (`crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`)\n- `#2310` (`assets/scripts/cam.d.ts`, `crates/app/src/script/mod.rs`)\n- `#2149` (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `site/content/guide/automate/mcp.md`)\n- `#2122` (`crates/app/src/lib.rs`)\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: Tool library import and export now support Tormach PathPilot (.csv) and Hurco WinMax (.TCM) tool tables with controller tool numbers, Hurco gauge lengths, and documentation (#2566)\nFixes #2566\n",
